              {
                "author": {
                  "displayName": "daulettoibazar",
                  "id": 6191295,
                  "progressionOptOut": false,
                  "thumbnailUrl": "https://storage.googleapis.com/kaggle-avatars/thumbnails/6191295-kg.png?t=2026-04-17-16-02-32",
                  "tier": "CONTRIBUTOR",
                  "url": "/daulettoibazar"
                },
                "authorType": "COMMENT",
                "competitionRanking": 3,
                "content": "<p>Assuming model encounters this sample in inference time, applying abs(rev(a) - rev(b)) = output:</p>\n<p>abs(rev(34) - rev(44)) = 1 correct 🟩\nabs(rev(41) - rev(32)) = 9 correct 🟩</p>\n<p>which leads to\nabs(rev(69) - rev(52)) = 71 incorrect 🟥 </p>\n<p>This indicates that the issue is not a case of multiple valid solution paths converging on the same final answer. Instead, different solution approaches can lead to different answers, which makes the problem insufficiently represented in the dataset. The only way to reliably obtain the specific ground-truth answer provided here would be to train directly on this formulation and effectively overfit to it.</p>",
                "feedbackTrackingData": {},
                "id": 3454544,
                "isThankYou": false,
                "kernelVersion": 0,
                "parent": {},
                "postDate": "2026-05-07T12:43:49.427Z",
                "rawMarkdown": "Assuming model encounters this sample in inference time, applying abs(rev(a) - rev(b)) = output:\n\nabs(rev(34) - rev(44)) = 1 correct 🟩\nabs(rev(41) - rev(32)) = 9 correct 🟩\n\nwhich leads to\nabs(rev(69) - rev(52)) = 71 incorrect 🟥 \n\nThis indicates that the issue is not a case of multiple valid solution paths converging on the same final answer. Instead, different solution approaches can lead to different answers, which makes the problem insufficiently represented in the dataset. The only way to reliably obtain the specific ground-truth answer provided here would be to train directly on this formulation and effectively overfit to it.",
