        "authorType": "COMMENT",
        "competitionRanking": 178,
        "content": "<pre><code> def _extract_last_boxed(text: str) -&gt; str | None:\n        if not starts:\n            return None\n        start = starts[-1]\n        depth = 1\n        i = start\n        while i &lt; len(text):\n            c = text[i]\n            if c == \"{\":\n                depth += 1\n            elif c == \"}\":\n                depth -= 1\n                if depth == 0:\n                    if text[i + 1 :].strip():\n                        return None\n                    return text[start:i]\n            i += 1\n        return None\n</code></pre>\n<p>Hi <a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/ryanholbrook\" target=\"_blank\">@ryanholbrook</a>, the metric regex \\boxed{([^}]*)(?:}|$) stops at the first }. In cryptarithm puzzles { and } can be valid answer characters — about 20% of cryptarithm puzzles in train.csv (169/823) have such answers and can never be marked correct.</p>",
        "feedbackTrackingData": {},
        "id": 3452165,
        "isThankYou": false,
        "kernelVersion": 0,
        "parent": {},
        "postDate": "2026-05-02T17:57:23.663Z",
        "rawMarkdown": "```python\n def _extract_last_boxed(text: str) -> str | None:\n        if not starts:\n            return None\n        start = starts[-1]\n        depth = 1\n        i = start\n        while i < len(text):\n            c = text[i]\n            if c == \"{\":\n                depth += 1\n            elif c == \"}\":\n                depth -= 1\n                if depth == 0:\n                    if text[i + 1 :].strip():\n                        return None\n                    return text[start:i]\n            i += 1\n        return None\n```\n\nHi @ryanholbrook, the metric regex \\\\boxed\\{([^}]*)(?:\\}|$) stops at the first }. In cryptarithm puzzles { and } can be valid answer characters — about 20% of cryptarithm puzzles in train.csv (169/823) have such answers and can never be marked correct.\n",
